{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Pushed — Gerrit change 3009\n\nCommit `2da950d6b99`, Change-Id `Ib9420b6a9ba6cb62d29ac6911e5ed189ad2ba981`.\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/3009\n\n## `make verify`: clean\n\n`34 failed, 20335 passed, 80 skipped in 1811.15s`. **Zero failures attributable to this\nchange.** The 34 break down as 17 known-environmental pandoc failures plus 17 that were an\nartifact of my own venv, described below.\n\nWorth noting for the baseline: the expected 18th failure,\n`test_completion_gate.py::test_file_impact_close_fetches_before_rejecting_stale_clone`\n(bug 9753-647b), **no longer fails** — change 2989 has merged.\n\n## The 17 extra failures were mine, not the tree's\n\nEvery test in `tests/unit/test_audit_ticket_page.py` and\n`tests/unit/test_audit_ticket_page_heldout.py` failed with:\n\n    src/rebar/audit/server.py:47: ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'jinja2'\n\nCause: to exercise these opcert tests at all I had to install the `reviewbot` extra\n(`fastapi` + `httpx`), because `tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py` opens with\n`pytest.importorskip(\"fastapi\")` and `make install` does not pull that extra — so on a bare\nworktree **all 10 of these tests silently skip**, and a local green run on this file means\nnothing.\n\nThe audit-page tests guard on `fastapi` and `httpx` but their render path also needs\n`jinja2`, which ships in the `[ui]` extra rather than `[reviewbot]`. Installing one extra\ntherefore un-skipped tests whose remaining dependency was still missing.\n\nConfirmed by installing `jinja2` and re-running exactly those two files: **17 passed**. So\nthis is an artifact of a partial-extra install I created, not a defect in the tree and not a\nregression from this change — under any sanctioned install matrix (`[ui]`, or CI's full\ninstall) the dependency is present. Not filing a ticket for it; the guard is correct for the\ninstall combinations the project actually supports.\n\n## Verification summary\n\n- 10/10 in `tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py`; the regression test hits its 0.2s bound.\n- Regression test confirmed to FAIL (hang to the suite budget) against the incorrect\n  `asyncio.timeout` implementation, so it genuinely guards the property.\n- `make check` green; `make verify` clean of real failures.\n\nUnverified: that the py3.11 `node down` crash itself stops recurring. It never reproduced\nlocally across 100 runs on 3.11.16/3.11.15/3.12.14, so this change is justified as a fix for\na separate and provable defect — an unbounded teardown join plus a budget that violated\npyproject's documented requirement — whose effect is to make the underlying race **legible**\nrather than to mask it. If the race recurs, it will now surface as a named assertion instead\nof a dead xdist worker.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789913512902409776,"uuid":"4ac09626-d24b-4c30-bfb1-98704071f85a"}